{"title":"What I’ve been reading","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/912111491/0/marginalrevolution~What-Ive-been-reading.html","date":1738473468000,"content":"<p>Owen Hatherley, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Militant-Modernism-Zero-Books-Hatherley/dp/1846941768/ref=sr_1_1?crid=R7JU23MVAQ0W&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.sYepjRC91TwS23VrVQtCvl2akSGePH-XcKlGybNFc53gQUbrqpqablpysYDhnR0eejbj-RYBEJkp1mjpGzmqGw.JeG709L18LZ-ru7-9bgbSIAvsthup4JRPTFfVvPBOws&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Owen+Hatherley%2C+Militant+Modernism&amp;qid=1738469145&amp;sprefix=owen+hatherley%2C+militant+modernism%2Caps%2C69&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Militant Modernism</a>.  A very good short book, defending “left wing modernism,” a much maligned target on the right these days.  Hatherley himself is a much underrated figure, a commie who came along at the wrong time but a very good writer and thinker about aesthetics.</p>\r\n<p>Stuart A. Reid, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Lumumba-Plot-Secret-History-Assassination/dp/1524748811/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3ARR8PR8C7QA5&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.r2lrCNuhi24iCiONMvDXjg.dqO6da1Tp66U449LqBiN2dW7-AN_83zfJRovkOnitk0&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Lumumba+Plot%3A+The+Secret+History+of+the+CIA+and+a+Cold+War+Assassination&amp;qid=1738469196&amp;sprefix=the+lumumba+plot+the+secret+history+of+the+cia+and+a+cold+war+assassination%2Caps%2C74&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Lumumba Plot: The Secret History of the CIA and a Cold War Assassination</a>.  For whatever reason, there are more good books about the Congo than most other parts of Africa.  This is one of them.  From 2023, but good enough to make a “best of non-fiction” list for a typical year.  Very cleanly written as well.</p>\r\n<p>Charles Callan Tansill, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Purchase-Danish-West-Indies-Diplomatic/dp/B004FP5YM0/ref=sr_1_1?crid=34A5Q3DSPJ5II&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.6ASENHzyWx9qQIhL6oa2yRraJ9_y7wj7eBgKpAC80sTx3iFFuxkpikL2Dc3jCnqf8vWzRlQ6O93pMT5_9kXW_Q.xNA84HAD-_iAkZaUv7Lzdogo3ID1EW47vG5YmU_kMbY&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Purchase+of+the+Danish+West+Indies&amp;qid=1738469250&amp;sprefix=the+purchase+of+the+danish+west+indies%2Caps%2C64&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Purchase of the Danish West Indies</a>.  Who would have thought that this 1966 volume, and Tansill, would be making a comeback?  The biggest lesson for me here was how much the purchase was a live issue as early as 1867.  And as the final purchase approached in 1917, the other European powers were by no means happy.</p>\r\n<p>Richard Overy, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Rain-Ruin-Tokyo-Hiroshima-Surrender/dp/1324105305/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2LXJXYSPXK66Y&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.vdsoP5kJKK5GJLtaSxDLKA.KcCFfMvI8vCAv5aOHncizUZjQjUSBtJJPtE2_4fhg5M&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Rain+of+Ruin%3A+Tokyo%2C+Hiroshima%2C+and+the+Surrender+of+Japan&amp;qid=1738469290&amp;sprefix=rain+of+ruin+tokyo%2C+hiroshima%2C+and+the+surrender+of+japan%2Caps%2C78&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Rain of Ruin: Tokyo, Hiroshima, and the Surrender of Japan</a> is a short but very good and substantive look at the non-nuclear and also nuclear bombing campaigns.</p>\r\n<p>Michael Krielaars, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.co.uk/Sound-Utopia-Musicians-Time-Stalin/dp/1805330020/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1KYOHI76LM29D&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.SJjvUnwTgBo-k7RYm5Qqpg.H9VXlpcVFeJRV9Uj3gDZbO64j3-z2rJRmetvXj_1ctw&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Sound+of+Utopia%3A+Musicians+in+the+Time+of+Stalin&amp;qid=1738469674&amp;sprefix=the+sound+of+utopia+musicians+in+the+time+of+stalin%2Caps%2C140&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Sound of Utopia: Musicians in the Time of Stalin</a>.  A surprisingly fresh and substantive book, which also does a good job integrating the first-person perspective of the author.  I’ve read the standard biographies of Shostokovich, Prokofiev, and the like, and still learned a lot from this one.</p>\r\n<p>There is Gregor Craigie, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Our-Crumbling-Foundation-Canadas-Housing/dp/1039009387/ref=sr_1_1?crid=RC0ULGB2Q5ON&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.3oqiUO85J59i1lEeTQXpVw.F7tredM1RdfmS3lMeNUhIbI54or4WPpeSCsPLic4LC4&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Our+Crumbling+Foundation%3A+How+We+Solve+Canada%27s+Housing+Crisis&amp;qid=1738469780&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=our+crumbling+foundation+how+we+solve+canada%27s+housing+crisis%2Cstripbooks%2C63&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">Our Crumbling Foundation: How We Solve Canada’s Housing Crisis</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Molly Worthen, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Spellbound-Charisma-American-History-Puritans/dp/0593729005/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2MQIRUCI3B6NI&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.p_sXVA9oCvI63x3qU_OwCQ.dhvrwoc77x67qAs6D-lqGhOsDoZtA8hBoSp2uiGsPro&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Spellbound%3A+How+Charisma+Shaped+American+History+From+the+Puritans+to+Donald+Trump&amp;qid=1738469925&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=spellbound+how+charisma+shaped+american+history+from+the+puritans+to+donald+trump%2Cstripbooks%2C59&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">Spellbound: How Charisma Shaped American History From the Puritans to Donald Trump</a> is a very good book on an underexplored topic.  In some ways tech has mattered less than you might think.</p>\r\n<p>Stephen Witt, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Thinking-Machine-Jensen-Coveted-Microchip/dp/0593832698/ref=sr_1_1?crid=25WXEU1YT4OVU&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.xyNgAvjxCZcxiZVdJTV5aA.f7T35Y1utCFeIqTQqnsV64wHUG3nYsnai79zkERu5Rs&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Thinking+Machine%3A+Jensen+Huang%2C+Nvidia%2C+and+the+World%27s+Most+Coveted+Microchip&amp;qid=1738469962&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=the+thinking+machine+jensen+huang%2C+nvidia%2C+and+the+world%27s+most+coveted+microchip%2Cstripbooks%2C63&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Thinking Machine: Jensen Huang, Nvidia, and the World’s Most Coveted Microchip</a>.  A fun and well-informed look at its subject matter.  There should be more books on one of the world’s most valuable companies, and yes here supply is elastic.</p>\r\n<p>Marc Hijink, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Focus-Inside-struggle-complex-machine/dp/B0D7DRJL2W/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1EWC9ZOWR70L4&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.ocEuegzMHfi1--bfCXdKDmQtyXHLnP43iJHf5dWuzE0.DznYYacDYxISYvfrA2gP2oL2NaW2JgZHCrjRikPwfqk&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Focus%3A+The+ASML+Way%2C+Inside+the+Power+Struggle+Over+the+Most+Complex+Machine+on+Earth&amp;qid=1738470055&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=focus+the+asml+way%2C+inside+the+power+struggle+over+the+most+complex+machine+on+earth%2Cstripbooks%2C58&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">Focus: The ASML Way, Inside the Power Struggle Over the Most Complex Machine on Earth</a>.  You have to already want to read a book about ASML, but this is in fact the relevant book about ASML.  To call it boring is to miss the point, because the company itself is somewhat boring.</p>\r\n<p>Jeanette zu Furstenberg, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.de/-/en/Wie-sind-zeigt-sich-Krisenzeiten/dp/3492073212/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1BXOKLLJ41VJ4&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.BvP2XgeJSOFydOzcPwwRMNBAz2Pt0EtIvrzjFNBdsdxMh3u5Br6k6Hgm4VF__2JZ4dcR1OaXydfChritEFbXtZ-Ncc4Gwm0sa5eQHJKWqpzyBa11iZqTKaGFj-mVzPATE9flrDGT5J5HX6OUnT2A4w.O_mlKjF-2WtisjL90muaIZS8eBFON5EigCkBMluztKU&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Wie+gut+wir+sind%2C+zeigt+sich+in+Krisenzeiten%3A+Ein+Weckruf&amp;qid=1738470334&amp;sprefix=wie+gut+wir+sind+zeigt+sich+in+krisenzeiten+ein+weckruf%2Caps%2C134&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Wie gut wir sind, zeigt sich in Krisenzeiten: Ein Weckruf</a>.  Exactly the wake-up call Germany needs.</p>\r\n<p>Rainer Zitelmann, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Origins-Poverty-Wealth-Rainer-Zitelmann/dp/1852527951\" target=\"_blank\">The Origins of Poverty and Wealth: My World Tour and Insights from the Global Libertarian Movement</a> is a kind of travel memoir from a man who has become one of our most prolific writers on behalf of liberty.</p>\r\n<p>And I was reading <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/EphieBernstein/status/1878500962123526623\" target=\"_blank\">my own short commentary on Atlas Shrugged</a>, from a few years ago.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/what-ive-been-reading-265.html\">What I’ve been reading</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/912111491/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/912111491/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/912111491/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/912111491/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/912111491/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/912111491/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/what-ive-been-reading-265.html#comments\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://asse